
=== Does 0x07 bit 0 fire an I2C read, or clear a FIFO id? (#33) ===

clock     : 320 MHz sys
sensor id : 0x82

-- bring-up --
  sensor id : 0x82  (legacy table)
  firmware  : 2023-03-03, fpga rev 32
  luma before anything is fired: 80

-- the space at rest, three dumps, nothing fired --
  registers that moved on their own: none

-- stage A: fire a read at 12 addresses, three visits, up down up --
  visit 0 done
  visit 1 done
  visit 2 done

  reg    per-address means, all 12              spread   scatter  retrace
  0b^    00 00 00 00 00 00 00 30 30 30 30 31    49       0        yes   (the probe writes this one)
  0c^    00 01 02 03 0a 1c 1d 00 02 0a 0b 00    29       0        yes   (the probe writes this one)
  48     00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 36 4c 02    76       0        yes   <- A1 and A2

  the space is 7 bits: 0x80-0xff mirrored 0x00-0x7f in all of 4608 reads

-- did firing it break the capture path? --
  luma after 36 fires: 106

  stage A names register 0x48.

-- stage B: does anything read through it track an exposure we control? --
  attempt 1: CAM_AUTO_WB straight onto the board, no re-enable
  handle ladder 1, six exposures doubling from 0x00010 to 0x00200:
    up    115 120 120 120 120 120
    down  120 120 120 120 120 120
    worst wobble 1, worst retrace 5
    H1 rises at every rung by more than the wobble: NO
    H2 the descent retraces within the wobble:      NO
    SO STAGE B HAS NONE
  attempt 1 found none. Attempt 2: the old warm-up, CAM_AUTO_ALL and
  twenty captures first, exactly as it used to run.
  handle ladder 2, six exposures doubling from 0x00010 to 0x00200:
    up    130 130 130 130 130 130
    down  130 130 130 130 130 130
    worst wobble 0, worst retrace 0
    H1 rises at every rung by more than the wobble: NO
    H2 the descent retraces within the wobble:      yes
    SO STAGE B HAS NONE

RESULT : stage A names 0x48, and STAGE B COULD NOT TEST IT. The two
         exposures did not part the picture, so the value stage B was
         going to look for was never put on the die. THIS IS NOT A VERDICT
         ON 0x48 EITHER WAY - do not read it as one, and do not adopt
         0x48 on stage A alone.
